This posting is an index of sources in the games archive on saab. It
differs from the archives at other archive sites in three respects:
1) All of the games are archived directly by game name without the
use of a volumeN directory, 2) Old (superseded) versions of games have
been removed to save disk space and 3) The archive also contains games
for X-Windows from comp.sources.x and the MIT tape that have not been
posted to comp.sources.games. The X games are provided as a service
for those sites that need a copy and don't have Internet ftp capability.

Index						2/6/93

This file contains a list of the games that are stored in the
comp.sources.games archive.  When retrieving the files, be sure
to add a '.Z' suffix to the end of the file name, as all of the
files are stored in 16-bit compress format, unless stated otherwise.
Also prepend the directory you used to get this file (currently
"/usr1/ftp/games-archive/").
